-- Dialogue: `show dialog "text" [at X, Y]` sets the `dialog` var (the game gates on
-- it), `show choice "a" "b" … [at X, Y]` draws buttons and keeps `choice` up to date,
-- and `when player talks to "NAME-OR-TAG"` is the trigger. Nothing pauses the engine.
wizard is {x: 40, y: 40}
wizard are talkers
show dialog "Hello, traveler!"
show dialog "Second line" at 4, 60
show choice "ask about quest" "leave"
show choice "yes" "no" at 8, 20

when player talks to "wizard"
  said is said + 1
when player talks to npc "talkers" show dialog "hi" at 1, 1
